<section class="block">
  <div class="wrap article-grid">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Who it is for</h2>
      <p>Charities and social purpose organisations that are considering earned income from selling services, products, expertise or assets. You may already have ideas, or you may know you need to diversify and have no idea where to start. Both are fine.</p>
      <h2>Why a review, not a business plan</h2>
      <p>Most small charities have no spare capacity. A plan that relies on a fully committed chief executive becoming a part-time consultant is not a plan. Before anyone writes a business plan, the Board needs to know what the market will pay for, who would do the work, and what would stop if they did.</p>
      <div class="qa-list">
        <div class="qa"><h3>What is the review?</h3><p>An independent, evidence-led assessment of whether commercial income is realistic for your organisation, with your own ideas tested against the market and a wider look for opportunities you have not considered.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <aside class="aside">
      <h2>Not sure it is for you?</h2>
      <p>Take the ten-question readiness quiz, or book a free call and we will tell you straight.</p>
      <p><a class="btn btn-black btn-small" href="#quiz">Take the quiz</a></p>
      <p><a class="btn btn-ghost btn-small" href="{{ site.calendly }}" rel="noopener">Book a call</a></p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block on-soft">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head"><h2>What it is, and what it is not</h2></div>
    <div class="grid g2">
      <div class="quote-card light">
        <h3>What the review is</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>An independent, evidence-led assessment of whether commercial income is realistic.</li>
          <li>A test of your ideas against the market, plus a wider look for ones you have not considered.</li>
          <li>An honest view of capacity: who would actually do this, and what would stop.</li>
          <li>Ballpark investment, income potential and risks for the strongest options.</li>
          <li>A clear recommendation, including "not now" or "not this" where the evidence says so.</li>
          <li>A trustee decision paper and Board presentation.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="quote-card light">
        <h3>What it is not</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>A business plan, implementation plan or marketing plan.</li>
          <li>A fully costed financial model.</li>
          <li>A guarantee that any option will generate income.</li>
          <li>A general fundraising or grants review.</li>
          <li>Legal, tax or VAT advice. We flag issues and signpost you to professional advisers.</li>
          <li>Us running, selling or marketing the new activity.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block on-black">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head"><h2>Two ways in</h2><p>Always look wider: even if you arrive with ideas, we bring at least two alternatives into the appraisal. The idea a charity arrives with is often not the one with the best fit.</p></div>
    <div class="grid g2">
      <div class="tile tile-dark"><h3>"We have ideas"</h3><p>You are already exploring one or more ideas, such as selling training or consultancy, and need to know if they are realistic. We test fewer ideas in more depth.</p></div>
      <div class="tile tile-yellow"><h3>"We don't know where to start"</h3><p>You want to diversify income and see enterprise as part of the picture. We audit your assets and capabilities, and build a long list from there.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head"><h2>How it works</h2><p>The review follows the Strategic Insight Model™, so by the time trustees see the recommendation they have already seen, scored and challenged the evidence behind it.</p></div>
    <ol class="method">
      <li><h3>Discover</h3><p>Agree the decision question and your red lines. Establish what you can afford, resource and legally do.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Listen</h3><p>Up to six internal interviews, and an audit of your assets, capabilities and appetite for commerce.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Interpret</h3><p>Scan the market, widen the lens and screen the long list to a shortlist for testing.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Challenge</h3><p>Six to eight conversations with people who would buy, fund or compete with each option.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Prioritise</h3><p>Trustees and senior leaders score the options in a workshop. We develop the top three.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Align</h3><p>A trustee decision paper, a Board presentation and a follow-up call about six weeks later.</p></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block on-yellow">
  <div class="wrap quote-hero">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Why it matters</p>
      <h2>A "no" that saved months of effort.</h2>
      <p class="lead">In a recent review for New Dawn New Day, a Leicester women's charity, staff were keen to sell consultancy on trauma-informed practice. Market conversations quickly showed that an established local provider had held that market for five years.</p>
      <p>The Board closed the idea down with confidence and redirected its energy. That is exactly the kind of result this review exists to deliver.</p>
      <a class="btn btn-black" href="/work/new-dawn-new-day">Read the New Dawn New Day case study</a>
    </div>
    <blockquote class="bigquote">
      <p>Matthew came in as a critical friend, and that is exactly what he was.</p>
      <cite>Sarah Nelson <span>Chair of Trustees, New Dawn New Day</span></cite>
    </blockquote>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head"><h2>What your Board decides</h2><p>The decision paper is written in Board-paper format, with the decisions required on the front page. For each of the top three options, trustees choose one of four outcomes.</p></div>
    <div class="grid g4">
      <div class="quote-card light"><h3>Proceed</h3><p>Commission a detailed business plan and financial model.</p></div>
      <div class="quote-card light"><h3>Pilot</h3><p>Test at small scale, with success measures and a review date.</p></div>
      <div class="quote-card light"><h3>Park</h3><p>Not now. Revisit when a stated trigger is met.</p></div>
      <div class="quote-card light"><h3>Stop</h3><p>Close the idea down and redirect energy elsewhere.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="prose" style="margin-top:2rem">
      <p>Options are judged against criteria agreed before any ideas are discussed, which takes the heat out of favourite projects. Every option passes three gateway tests first (fit with your mission, your red lines, and what your charity is permitted to do), then is scored on market demand, competitive position, financial potential, capacity, mission synergy, investment, risk and time to income. Investment and income are given in honest bands, not false precision.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block on-soft" id="quiz">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head"><h2>Is your charity ready to explore earned income?</h2><p>Ten statements. Score each: Yes (2), Partly (1) or No (0). Be hard on yourself; the result is only useful if it is honest.</p></div>
    <form class="quiz" id="readiness-quiz" onsubmit="return false">
      {% set qs = [
        "We have at least one service, skill, product or asset that people outside our beneficiaries value.",
        "We know the full cost of delivering our current services.",
        "We have unrestricted reserves we could invest in, and potentially lose on, a new venture.",
        "Someone has, or could be freed up to have, the time to lead a new income stream.",
        "Our trustees are open to commercial activity and understand that it carries risk.",
        "We have, or could access, sales, marketing or commercial skills.",
        "We have relationships with organisations that might buy from us.",
        "We are clear what we would never do to earn income.",
        "We could wait 12 to 24 months for a new income stream to make a real contribution.",
        "Our reason for exploring enterprise goes beyond \"we need money now\"."
      ] %}
      {% for q in qs %}
      <fieldset class="quiz-q">
        <legend><span>{{ loop.index }}</span> {{ q }}</legend>
        <label><input type="radio" name="q{{ loop.index }}" value="2"> Yes</label>
        <label><input type="radio" name="q{{ loop.index }}" value="1"> Partly</label>
        <label><input type="radio" name="q{{ loop.index }}" value="0"> No</label>
      </fieldset>
      {% endfor %}
      <p class="quiz-progress" id="quiz-progress" aria-live="polite">Answer all ten to see your result.</p>
      <div class="quiz-result" id="quiz-result" hidden aria-live="polite">
        <p class="quiz-score"><strong id="quiz-total">0</strong> out of 20</p>
        <h3 id="quiz-title"></h3>
        <p id="quiz-text"></p>
        <p><a class="btn btn-black" href="{{ site.calendly }}" rel="noopener" id="quiz-cta">Book a free 30-minute call</a></p>
      </div>
    </form>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="block">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head"><h2>Questions</h2></div>
    <div class="qa-grid">
      {% for item in faq %}<div class="qa"><h3>{{ item.q }}</h3><p>{{ item.a }}</p></div>{% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% include "cta.njk" %}

<script>
(function () {
  var form = document.getElementById('readiness-quiz');
  if (!form) return;
  var bands = [
    { min: 14, title: "You look well placed to explore enterprise", text: "An Income Opportunity Review would help you identify and test the strongest options, and give your Board a clear decision." },
    { min: 8, title: "Some foundations are there", text: "A review, or a short conversation, would help clarify whether now is the right time and where to start." },
    { min: 0, title: "Enterprise may not be the right focus just now", text: "A conversation about your fundraising strategy may be more useful: do you have one, what is in it, is there a case for support, and are you covering every strand?" }
  ];
  function update() {
    var total = 0, answered = 0;
    for (var i = 1; i <= 10; i++) {
      var c = form.querySelector('input[name="q' + i + '"]:checked');
      if (c) { answered++; total += parseInt(c.value, 10); }
    }
    var res = document.getElementById('quiz-result'), prog = document.getElementById('quiz-progress');
    if (answered < 10) { res.hidden = true; prog.hidden = false; prog.textContent = answered + ' of 10 answered.'; return; }
    var b = bands.filter(function (x) { return total >= x.min; })[0];
    document.getElementById('quiz-total').textContent = total;
    document.getElementById('quiz-title').textContent = b.title;
    document.getElementById('quiz-text').textContent = b.text;
    prog.hidden = true; res.hidden = false;
  }
  form.addEventListener('change', update);
})();
</script>

